+++ b/README.md
@@ -24,6 +24,38 @@ input throws `InvalidTaskError`, which carries the position of the first
 invalid item in `index`. All library errors extend `TaskPlanError` and have a
 `code`.

+## Planning
+
+The planning feature is exported from `src/index.ts`.
+
+```ts
+import { planOrder, DuplicateTaskError, UnknownDependencyError, CycleError } from "./src/index.ts";
+```
+
+`planOrder(tasks)` returns a `PlanResult` with `order: string[]` and `stages: string[][]`.
+
+* `order` is built one task at a time, picking the highest `priority` among ready tasks and breaking ties by input position. As soon as a task is placed, newly unblocked tasks compete immediately.
+* `stages[k]` contains tasks whose earliest round is `k`, ordered by priority then input position. A task with no dependencies is in round 0; others are in `1 + max` of their dependencies.
+* Errors are checked in order: `DuplicateTaskError` with `code "DUPLICATE_ID"` and `taskIds`, `UnknownDependencyError` with `code "UNKNOWN_DEPENDENCY"`, `taskId` and `dependency`, and `CycleError` with `code "CYCLE"` and `cycle`. All extend `TaskPlanError`.
+
+CLI usage:
+
+```bash
+node src/cli.ts plan tasks.json
+node src/cli.ts plan tasks.json --json
+```
+
+Default output prints stages counted from 1 then the order, e.g.:
+
+```
+Stage 1: docs, compile
+Stage 2: test
+Stage 3: package
+Order: docs, compile, test, package
+```
+
+See the runnable demo in `examples/basic.ts` which uses the SPEC.md example tasks.
+
 ## Development

 Requires Node.js 24 or later. TypeScript files run directly with Node.
